title: 'Windows release blockers from PR #52 worked through (draft PR #53)'
summary: |-
  On feat/gnomon-windows-release (draft PR #53 → feat/gnomon) the PR #52 release blockers were closed, each Aegis-reviewed before commit:
  - **Aegis H1:** a session's objects admit that session only. Its default DACL is own-SID allow, then a Gnomon-SID deny, then user/SY, then OW RC; --low requires --session-sid. Falsifier: kill, probe and WRITE_DAC are all EPERM.
  - **Aegis M3:** process.confine lowers only a direct child of the asking process, created after it, never the helper itself. The job comes before the integrity drop, and the endpoint refuses an exited child.
  - **W1 probes:** P01 partial, log-fsync pass, P11 partial, P14b-w partial, P10w fail. Non-elevated WFP is denied, so network denies need the W11 service.
  - **W3:** write-through durable renames and a real boot id (win:<n>). Windows process control uses launcher-job groups and creation-time witnesses, with process.terminate {pid,start}; the graceful stop closes stdin. A filtered session PATH plus NoDefaultCurrentDirectoryInExePath. Policy registry keys are read by API (registry.read), not localized reg.exe text.
  - **W5 acceptance:** a session cannot see, message or focus a Medium window.
  - **Hygiene:** one WIN32_HELPER_PROTOCOL; the per-op re-hash kept on measurement (0.36 ms vs 16 ms per spawn); a G-WIN-05 ratchet on inline platform branches in src/kernel.
  - **Spec and CHANGELOG:** §15.5/§16 "Windows as built" and a CHANGELOG Windows section.
  - **Loops-on-Windows fixes:** two env-file fail-opens (a followed symlink; the owner check skipped on win32), humanBusyIn never matching on Windows, and host-path issues.

  Deferred: standing grants wait on helper screen-lock events (T-2026-10-23-002); shared ~/.claude/projects and named-object squatting (T-2026-10-23-001); W6 wrapper (SendInput test, browser-surface refusal); W7–W9 packaging.
