decisions:
  - id: win-group-is-launcher
    decision: On Windows the process 'group' is the session launcher pid whose kill-on-close job holds the tree; terminate only through the helper with the caller's recorded creation-time witness
    rationale: Windows has no process groups; a bare pid can be recycled during the grace window (Aegis M1/H1); a snapshot must never become the witness
  - id: win-graceful-stdin
    decision: Windows graceful stop closes stdin instead of SIGTERM
    rationale: node maps SIGTERM to TerminateProcess; exec.rs's staged stop is control message, stdin close, kill
  - id: keep-rehash
    decision: Keep re-hashing the helper before every op
    rationale: measured 0.36 ms vs ~16 ms per spawn; a cached hash would reopen the swap window
  - id: standing-needs-lock-events
    decision: Do not enable Windows standing grants until the helper reports screen lock
    rationale: grants must end at lock; signing their uses in click mode without lock events would let a grant outlive a locked screen
learnings:
  - SDDL alias spelling, elevated BA ownership and token default owner all bit owner-only checks on the GitHub Windows runner
  - 'A snapshot that writes witness state lets a recycled pid inherit trust: pass witnesses explicitly from the recording site'
  - 'On Windows O_NOFOLLOW is 0: any open-without-follow code needs an lstat refusal there'
  - Git Bash collapses \\ in heredocs; write backslash-bearing TS with the Edit tool or String.fromCharCode(92)
